    "result_text": "All 285 tests pass with a green build. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created, the app now counts how many other owners already share the same last name at that moment and returns it as the integer field `namesakeCount` in the owner response.\n\nChanges made, following the existing pattern used for `membershipNumber`/`membershipTier`:\n\n1. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 for new owners, sets `namesakeCount` via a new `countNamesakes(owner)` helper that counts existing owners whose last name matches (case- and whitespace-insensitive, reusing the existing `normalize` helper). It runs before the new owner is persisted, so it reflects only pre-existing namesakes.\n\n2. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a persisted `namesake_count` column with getter/setter, so the value is stored and returned on later `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads (which the acceptance test relies on).\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to all four schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema; the generated `OwnerDto` and MapStruct mapper pick it up automatically by name.\n\nThe provided `Cp16Tests` (first owner with a surname \u2192 0, second \u2192 1) passes, and the full suite is green (285 tests).",
